<h1>Matt Brewer</h1>
<p>Trial lawyer, former CHA board chair. Candidate for mayor of Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p>Partner at the law firm Bartlit Beck, former chair and interim CEO of the Chicago Housing Authority, and co-owner of The Wiener&#39;s Circle; 46, raised by his mother in Grand Crossing, Stanford&#39;s first Black student body president, Yale Law. Filed on the first day.</p>
<p><a href="/directdemocracy/app/candidate/yEOHKeU0AAQnb91496PDiIjOmZg2">Full platform, open to comments</a></p>
<p><a href="https://www.mattbrewer.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website (mattbrewer.com)</a></p>
<h2>Campaign money</h2>
<ul>
<li>Committee: Brewer for Chicago</li>
<li>Raised: $405K</li>
<li>Spent: $271K</li>
<li>Cash on hand: $239K</li>
<li>Since the committee formed June 25, 2026, through Sept. 30. <a href="https://elections.il.gov/CampaignDisclosure/CommitteeDetail.aspx?id=41238" rel="nofollow noopener">Source</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Money figures are each committee&#39;s quarterly reports to the Illinois State Board of Elections: spent is total expenditures from January 1 to September 30, 2026 (or since the committee formed), cash is funds available on September 30.</p>
<h2>Support</h2>
<p>0.1% of likely voters in the ChicagoSpeaks poll, Sept. 2026 (Mansueto Institute / NORC). 0.4 points of support per $1 million spent.</p>
<h2>What they would do</h2>
<ul>
<li>Rejects the choice between supporting police and investing in neighborhoods: do both. <q>For too long, we&#39;ve been presented with a false choice about Chicago&#39;s future.</q> (<a href="https://blockclubchicago.org/2026/10/26/who-is-running-for-chicago-mayor/" rel="nofollow noopener">Block Club Chicago, Oct. 26, 2026</a>)</li>
<li>Attract businesses and jobs while investing in overlooked communities. <q>We can invest in our people without sacrificing our competitive edge.</q> (<a href="https://blockclubchicago.org/2026/10/26/who-is-running-for-chicago-mayor/" rel="nofollow noopener">Block Club Chicago, Oct. 26, 2026</a>)</li>
<li>A child&#39;s future should not depend on their zip code: early help for students who fall behind and a plan for every CPS graduate. <q>A child&#39;s future should not be determined by their zipcode.</q> (<a href="https://www.mattbrewer.com/priorities" rel="nofollow noopener">mattbrewer.com</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>AI summary</h2>
<h3>Main points</h3>
<p>Housing: Make it easier to build homes at every price, put vacant land back to use, protect renters from displacement, and help homeowners on fixed incomes stay.</p>
<p>Growth: Grow the tax base with more residents, businesses, and jobs instead of raising taxes, and tie job training to the employers the city recruits.</p>
<p>Safety and schools: Well-trained, accountable police who solve more crimes, every city service concentrated on the most violent blocks, and early help for students who fall behind.</p>
<h3>Next to the others</h3>
<p>Only Brewer: Concentrating every city service, not only police, on the blocks with the most violence.</p>
<p>Taxes: Brewer, Mendoza, Holberg, Nee, and Wilson say relief comes from a bigger tax base; Johnson wants the ultra-rich to pay more.</p>
<p>Renters: Brewer and Cardenas stress protecting renters from displacement; Quigley rejects new rent restrictions.</p>
<h2>On money</h2>
<p>Says the city cannot tax its way to prosperity and that taxing businesses more would mean the city has failed; would grow the tax base with residents, businesses, and jobs instead.</p>
<ul>
<li><q>If the main source of revenue is taxing businesses, then taxing businesses more. Then, we&#39;ve failed,</q> (<a href="https://abc7chicago.com/post/former-chicago-housing-authority-cha-ceo-matt-brewer-announces-run-mayor/19381797/" rel="nofollow noopener">ABC7 Chicago, June 25, 2026</a>)</li>
<li><q>Chicago cannot tax its way to prosperity.</q> (<a href="https://www.mattbrewer.com/priorities" rel="nofollow noopener">mattbrewer.com</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pizza</h2>
<p>No position on record.</p>
<h2>Also on the record</h2>
<ul>
<li>Co-owns The Wiener&#39;s Circle, the hot dog stand famous for insulting its customers. (<a href="https://blockclubchicago.org/2026/09/29/wieners-circle-has-always-had-something-to-say-what-happens-when-its-owner-runs-for-mayor/" rel="nofollow noopener">blockclubchicago.org</a>)</li>
<li>Worked in the Chinese music industry in Beijing as a Luce fellow, and co-founded Chicago&#39;s first Black-owned cannabis dispensary with his mother and brother. (<a href="https://www.mattbrewer.com/about" rel="nofollow noopener">mattbrewer.com</a>)</li>
</ul>
